    "explanation": "Both sides end up in the same place, and the record supports it, so the rider's claim succeeds only in part and 1.10 SGD is returned.\n\nDeviation (POL-RD-22). On the platform's recorded distances the trip ran 9.4 km against a recommended route of 8.2 km, a deviation of 1.20 km, which is over the 1.0 km tolerance. The GPS trace is used only to show which route was taken and when, not to re-measure distance: after fixes on the PIE the vehicle is on Bedok North Road from 09:26:25 and Upper Changi Road from 09:30:25, rejoining Still Road at 09:33:55. Both parties accept the 1.20 km figure, and nothing in the record supports a longer or repeated deviation.\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23). The only traffic data for the recommended PIE segment (Bedok North Road to Still Road, towards Tuas), overlapping the trip window, is of type NONE, with no incident, roadwork or closure and speed bands 4-6. That is not congestion, an incident or a closure. Your explanation, driver, that the PIE stretch 'always crawls' is an assertion; POL-RD-23 says an assertion of traffic with no supporting data does not justify a reroute. The no-refund rows of the matrix are therefore not reached, and neither side presses them.\n\nNotice to the rider (POL-RD-21). A driver must tell the rider of a deviation by in-app chat, or verbally with a call recording. The chat log holds only two entries (09:17:50 and 09:18:15), both about the pickup meeting point and both before the trip started at 09:19:25; there are no messages during the trip and no in-app calls at all, and the deviation began at 09:26:44. Notice was not given, and any unrecorded verbal notice cannot be established (POL-GEN-26).\n\nOutcome (POL-RD-24). Row (d) applies: not traffic-justified, deviation over 1 km, so the excess distance fare is refunded in full. That fare is the deviation distance times the metered per-km rate: 1.20 km x 0.92 SGD = 1.10 SGD, no surge, rounded to the cent, which is also the figure the payments ledger's own derivation reaches. The rider asked for 4.00 SGD, but 4.00 is the contested sum (POL-GEN-22), not the remedy; the itemised metered fare carries base fare 3.80, distance fare 8.65, time fare 4.08 and platform fee 0.90 with zero surge and zero ERP, and no distance surcharge beyond the 9.4 km actually driven. So 1.10 SGD of the charge is returned and the rest of the metered charge stands; the rider is not entirely right, so the outcome is the partial refund POL-GEN-03 describes rather than a full one.\n\nConfidence and who decides (POL-RD-25, POL-GEN-22). The dispute value is 4.00 SGD, below 10.00 SGD, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence; POL-RD-25 nevertheless requires 0.80, and the deciding facts are carried by artifacts all at weight 1.0 (trip record, GPS trace, chat log, fare breakdown, traffic advisory), so the confidence below sits under that ceiling and above the bar. Route deviation has no referral clause, so none is added.",
